WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.815
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 1, Networking concepts, which is 23 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.815 --> 00:00:10.483
This lesson covers objective 1 point 5.

00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:14.383
Compare and contrast transmission media and transceivers.

00:00:14.383 --> 00:00:17.940
Today's concept: matching the cable to the distance.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.215
The question is a distance problem.

00:00:22.215 --> 00:00:27.550
You need ten gigabits per second, over more than one hundred meters, but less than five hundred.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.880
Copper, even Cat six A, tops out at one hundred meters.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:41.020
Multimode fiber, O M three and O M four, carries ten gigabit roughly three hundred to four hundred meters, and costs less than single-mode.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.846
Our target zone starts where copper ends.

00:00:43.846 --> 00:00:47.160
Multimode fiber covers it at the lowest sensible cost.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.788
Remember the pattern.

00:00:50.788 --> 00:00:52.935
Copper stops at one hundred meters.

00:00:52.935 --> 00:00:57.291
For ten gigabit past that and under five hundred, pick multimode fiber.

00:00:57.291 --> 00:00:59.377
Single-mode works, but costs more.

00:00:59.377 --> 00:01:01.340
That's objective one point five.
